.TH "GIT-BUG" "1" "Apr 2019" "Generated from git-bug's source code" ""

.SH NAME
git-bug-bug-review-add - Record a review on a pull-request


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgit-bug bug review add [BUG_ID] [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Record a review verdict (approve, request-changes, or comment) on a
pull-request. Exactly one of --approve / --request-changes / --comment must
be supplied. By default the review is anchored to the PR's current head
commit; override with --commit.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--approve\fP[=false]
	Approve the pull-request

.PP
\fB--request-changes\fP[=false]
	Request changes on the pull-request

.PP
\fB--comment\fP[=false]
	Leave a comment-only review (no verdict)

.PP
\fB-m\fP, \fB--message\fP=""
	Review body

.PP
\fB-F\fP, \fB--file\fP=""
	Take the review body from the given file (- for stdin)

.PP
\fB--commit\fP=""
	Commit hash the review is anchored to (defaults to the PR's head commit)

.PP
\fB--non-interactive\fP[=false]
	Do not ask for user input

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for add


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBgit-bug-bug-review(1)\fP
